**Proof.** We claim that for all $a, b > 0$,
$$\frac{a^{3}+3 b^{3}}{5 a+b} \geq \frac{25 b^{2}-a^{2}}{36}. \tag{1}$$

Indeed, since $5a+b>0$, (1) is equivalent to
$$36(a^{3}+3b^{3}) \geq (25b^{2}-a^{2})(5a+b),$$
i.e.
$$36a^{3}+108b^{3} \geq 125ab^{2}+25b^{3}-5a^{3}-a^{2}b,$$
which rearranges to
$$41a^{3}+a^{2}b-125ab^{2}+83b^{3} \geq 0.$$

Setting $s = a/b > 0$ and dividing by $b^{3}$, the left side becomes
$$41s^{3}+s^{2}-125s+83.$$
This factors as
$$41s^{3}+s^{2}-125s+83 = (s-1)^{2}(41s+83).$$

Since $s>0$, we have $41s+83>0$ and $(s-1)^{2}\geq 0$, so (1) holds, with equality iff $a=b$.

Applying (1) cyclically:
$$\frac{a^{3}+3 b^{3}}{5 a+b} \geq \frac{25 b^{2}-a^{2}}{36},\qquad \frac{b^{3}+3 c^{3}}{5 b+c} \geq \frac{25 c^{2}-b^{2}}{36},\qquad \frac{c^{3}+3 a^{3}}{5 c+a} \geq \frac{25 a^{2}-c^{2}}{36}.$$

Summing the three inequalities,
$$\sum_{\mathrm{cyc}}\frac{a^{3}+3 b^{3}}{5 a+b} \geq \frac{(25b^{2}-a^{2})+(25c^{2}-b^{2})+(25a^{2}-c^{2})}{36}=\frac{24(a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2})}{36}=\frac{2}{3}(a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2}).$$

Equality holds when $a=b=c$. $\blacksquare$

